IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), Part V: reconsideration (regs 78 and 79) and the suspension of
-- benefits pending an appeal (regs 80 to 82; regs 83 to 87 are repealed). Piece er5, LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Every `src:N` is a line of SOR-96-332.txt (the Regulations' raw file). The text is an unofficial rendering; nothing
-- here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Relations (Hohfeld), stated once each, neutrally: reg 78 is a condition on the power of a person to have a decision of the
-- Commission reconsidered under s 112 of the Act (the Commission is subject to that power, and bound by reg 79 to decide
-- without delay); regs 80 to 82 are the Commission's power to stop benefits being payable by appealing (the claimant is
-- liable to have them held back). The Act's own s 112 (the time limit and the right itself) is piece ei4's.

§ `Regulations Part V - Administrative Provisions`

§§ `Reconsideration under Section 112 of the Act - reg 78(1): what the request must contain`

-- A request for reconsideration of a decision of the Commission "must be in writing and contain the following information":
-- (a) the person's name and (i) social insurance number or business number, (ii) address and telephone number, (iii) facsimile number and email address, if any;
-- (b) the date the decision was communicated; (c) the reasons; (d) any relevant information not previously provided.
-- Each "if any" is read for the item it follows: a fax number is required only of a person who has one, an email address only of a person who has one.
-- src:1643 | 78 (1) For the purposes of section 112 of the Act, a request for reconsideration of a decision of the Commission must be in writing and contain the following information:
-- src:1644 | (a) the name of the person making the request and their
-- src:1645 | (i) social insurance number or the business number assigned to them by the Minister of National Revenue, as the case may be,
-- src:1646 | (ii) address and telephone number, and
-- src:1647 | (iii) facsimile number and email address, if any;
-- src:1648 | (b) the date on which the decision was communicated to the person;
-- src:1649 | (c) the reasons why the person is requesting a reconsideration of the decision; and
-- src:1650 | (d) any relevant information that was not previously provided to the Commission.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 78(1) (src:1643-1650)
GIVEN `the request is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request gives the name of the person making it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request gives that person's social insurance number or the business number assigned to them by the Minister of National Revenue` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request gives that person's address and telephone number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person has a facsimile number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request gives that person's facsimile number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person has an email address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request gives that person's email address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request gives the date on which the decision was communicated to that person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request gives the reasons why that person is requesting a reconsideration of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person has relevant information that was not previously provided to the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request contains that information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 78(1) the request for reconsideration is in writing and contains the information required` IF
        `the request is in writing`
    AND `the request gives the name of the person making it`
    AND `the request gives that person's social insurance number or the business number assigned to them by the Minister of National Revenue`
    AND `the request gives that person's address and telephone number`
    AND ((NOT `that person has a facsimile number`) OR `the request gives that person's facsimile number`)
    AND ((NOT `that person has an email address`) OR `the request gives that person's email address`)
    AND `the request gives the date on which the decision was communicated to that person`
    AND `the request gives the reasons why that person is requesting a reconsideration of the decision`
    AND ((NOT `that person has relevant information that was not previously provided to the Commission`) OR `the request contains that information`)

§§ `Reconsideration under Section 112 of the Act - reg 78(2): where it is filed`

-- Filed with the Commission "at the address, facsimile number or email address - or in accordance with the electronic filing procedure -
-- provided by the Commission on the website of the Department of Employment and Social Development": any one of the four.
-- src:1651 | (2) A request for reconsideration must be filed with the Commission at the address, facsimile number or email address — or in accordance with the electronic filing procedure — provided by the Commission on the website of the Department of Employment and Social Development.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 78(2) (src:1651)
GIVEN `the request was filed at the address that the Commission provides on the website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request was filed at the facsimile number that the Commission provides on the website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request was filed at the email address that the Commission provides on the website` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request was filed in accordance with the electronic filing procedure that the Commission provides on the website` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 78(2) the request for reconsideration was filed as the Commission's website provides` IF
        `the request was filed at the address that the Commission provides on the website`
    OR  `the request was filed at the facsimile number that the Commission provides on the website`
    OR  `the request was filed at the email address that the Commission provides on the website`
    OR  `the request was filed in accordance with the electronic filing procedure that the Commission provides on the website`

§§ `Reconsideration under Section 112 of the Act - reg 79: the decision without delay`

-- The Commission "must render decisions on requests for reconsideration without delay": the person who made a request holds a claim
-- to a decision, and the Commission is bound. The duty arises once a request for reconsideration has been made.
-- src:1652 | 79 The Commission must render decisions on requests for reconsideration without delay.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 79 (src:1652)
GIVEN `a request for reconsideration of a decision of the Commission has been made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 79 the Commission must render its decision on the request without delay` IF
    `a request for reconsideration of a decision of the Commission has been made`

-- "Without delay" is not given a number of days or any other measure, so whether the Commission has been too slow is not answered:
-- the rule returns NOTHING for every case (an explicit "not covered" value).
-- src:1652 | 79 The Commission must render decisions on requests for reconsideration without delay.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 79 (src:1652)
GIVEN `the number of days the Commission has taken since the request was made` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 79 the Commission has rendered its decision without delay` IS
    NOTHING

§§ `Suspension of Benefits Pending Appeal - reg 80`

-- Benefits "are not payable in accordance with a decision of the Employment Insurance Section ... or the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal"
-- if, "within 21 days after the day on which a decision is given", the Commission appeals to the Appeal Division on the ground of an error in law.
-- The appeal cannot come before the decision; an appeal on the very day the decision is given is counted (assumed, not ruled: fork F-reg80).
-- src:1655 | 80 Benefits are not payable in accordance with a decision of the Employment Insurance Section of the Social Security Tribunal or the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal established under section 43.01 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act if, within 21 days after the day on which a decision is given, the Commission appeals to the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal on the ground that the Employment Insurance Section or the Board of Appeal, as the case may be, has erred in law.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 80 (src:1655)
GIVEN `the day on which the decision of the Employment Insurance Section or the Board of Appeal is given` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the Commission appeals to the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal, if it does` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the Commission's ground is that the Employment Insurance Section or the Board of Appeal has erred in law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 80 benefits are not payable in accordance with the decision` IF
        `the Commission's ground is that the Employment Insurance Section or the Board of Appeal has erred in law`
    AND (   CONSIDER `the day on which the Commission appeals to the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal, if it does`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST appeal THEN     appeal AT LEAST `the day on which the decision of the Employment Insurance Section or the Board of Appeal is given`
                                  AND appeal AT MOST (`the last day of` 21 `days after` `the day on which the decision of the Employment Insurance Section or the Board of Appeal is given`))

§§ `Suspension of Benefits Pending Appeal - reg 81`

-- If the Commission applies under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of a decision of the Appeal Division, "benefits are not payable in respect of
-- the claim for benefits that is the object of the decision until the final determination of the application for judicial review."
-- src:1656 | 81 If the Commission makes an application under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of a decision of the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal, benefits are not payable in respect of the claim for benefits that is the object of the decision until the final determination of the application for judicial review.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 81 (src:1656)
GIVEN `the claim is the one that is the object of the decision of the Appeal Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has applied under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision of the Appeal Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application for judicial review has been finally determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 81 benefits are not payable in respect of the claim` IF
        `the claim is the one that is the object of the decision of the Appeal Division`
    AND `the Commission has applied under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision of the Appeal Division`
    AND (NOT `the application for judicial review has been finally determined`)

§§ `Suspension of Benefits Pending Appeal - reg 82: a decision that a provision is ultra vires`

-- The claims caught by regs 82(1) and 82(2) are the same two kinds: "the claim for benefits that is the object of the decision",
-- and "any other claim for benefits made after that decision, if benefits would not be payable except for that decision".
-- src:1657 | 82 (1) If either a decision of the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal that declares a provision of the Act or these Regulations to be ultra vires or a decision of the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal established under section 43.01 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act that declares a provision of these Regulations to be ultra vires is appealed by the Commission to the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal, benefits are not payable in respect of the claim for benefits that is the object of the decision — nor in respect of any other claim for benefits made after that decision, if benefits would not be payable except for that decision — until
-- src:1660 | (2) If the Commission makes an application under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of a decision of the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal that declares a provision of the Act or these Regulations to be ultra vires, benefits are not payable in respect of the claim for benefits that is the object of the decision — nor in respect of any other claim for benefits made after the decision of the Appeal Division, if benefits would not be payable except for that decision — until the final determination of the application for judicial review.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 82(1), reg 82(2) (src:1657) (src:1660)
GIVEN `the claim is the one that is the object of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim was made after the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `benefits would not be payable on the claim except for the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 82(1) and (2) the claim is caught by the decision` IF
        `the claim is the one that is the object of the decision`
    OR (    `the claim was made after the decision`
        AND `benefits would not be payable on the claim except for the decision`)

-- (1) Either a decision of the General Division that declares a provision of the Act or the Regulations ultra vires, or a decision of the
-- Employment Insurance Board of Appeal that declares a provision of the Regulations ultra vires, is appealed by the Commission to the Appeal Division.
-- Benefits are then not payable on a caught claim until (a) the final determination of the appeal by the Appeal Division; or (b) the final determination of any
-- application by the Commission for judicial review of that determination, if the final determination of the appeal declares the provision ultra vires.
-- Reading taken (fork F-reg82): (b) lengthens the stoppage past (a) only when the Appeal Division's final determination declares the provision ultra vires and
-- the Commission has applied for judicial review of it; with no such application the stoppage ends at (a).
-- src:1657 | 82 (1) If either a decision of the General Division of the Social Security Tribunal that declares a provision of the Act or these Regulations to be ultra vires or a decision of the Employment Insurance Board of Appeal established under section 43.01 of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act that declares a provision of these Regulations to be ultra vires is appealed by the Commission to the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal, benefits are not payable in respect of the claim for benefits that is the object of the decision — nor in respect of any other claim for benefits made after that decision, if benefits would not be payable except for that decision — until
-- src:1658 | (a) the final determination of the appeal by the Appeal Division; or
-- src:1659 | (b) the final determination of any application made by the Commission under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the final determination of the appeal by the Appeal Division, if the final determination of the appeal declares the provision of the Act or these Regulations to be ultra vires.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 82(1) (src:1657-1659)
GIVEN `the decision is a decision of the General Division that declares a provision of the Act or the Regulations to be ultra vires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is a decision of the Board of Appeal that declares a provision of the Regulations to be ultra vires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has appealed the decision to the Appeal Division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is caught by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Appeal Division has made its final determination of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the final determination of the appeal declares the provision to be ultra vires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has applied under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the final determination of the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application for judicial review has been finally determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 82(1) benefits are not payable on the claim` IF
        (   `the decision is a decision of the General Division that declares a provision of the Act or the Regulations to be ultra vires`
         OR `the decision is a decision of the Board of Appeal that declares a provision of the Regulations to be ultra vires`)
    AND `the Commission has appealed the decision to the Appeal Division`
    AND `the claim is caught by the decision`
    AND (   (NOT `the Appeal Division has made its final determination of the appeal`)
         OR (    `the final determination of the appeal declares the provision to be ultra vires`
             AND `the Commission has applied under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the final determination of the appeal`
             AND (NOT `the application for judicial review has been finally determined`)))

-- (2) If the Commission applies under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of a decision of the Appeal Division that declares a provision of the Act
-- or the Regulations ultra vires, benefits are not payable on a caught claim until the final determination of the application.
-- src:1660 | (2) If the Commission makes an application under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of a decision of the Appeal Division of the Social Security Tribunal that declares a provision of the Act or these Regulations to be ultra vires, benefits are not payable in respect of the claim for benefits that is the object of the decision — nor in respect of any other claim for benefits made after the decision of the Appeal Division, if benefits would not be payable except for that decision — until the final determination of the application for judicial review.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 82(2) (src:1660)
GIVEN `the decision of the Appeal Division declares a provision of the Act or the Regulations to be ultra vires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commission has applied under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is caught by the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application for judicial review has been finally determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 82(2) benefits are not payable on the claim` IF
        `the decision of the Appeal Division declares a provision of the Act or the Regulations to be ultra vires`
    AND `the Commission has applied under the Federal Courts Act for judicial review of the decision`
    AND `the claim is caught by the decision`
    AND (NOT `the application for judicial review has been finally determined`)

§§ `Regs 83 to 87 - repealed`

-- Each of these five regulations reads only "[Repealed, SOR/2013-64, s. 2]". A labelled stub, with no operative outcome; nothing calls it.
-- src:1661 | 83 [Repealed, SOR/2013-64, s. 2]
-- src:1662 | 84 [Repealed, SOR/2013-64, s. 2]
-- src:1663 | 85 [Repealed, SOR/2013-64, s. 2]
-- src:1664 | 86 [Repealed, SOR/2013-64, s. 2]
-- src:1665 | 87 [Repealed, SOR/2013-64, s. 2]
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations regs 83 to 87 (src:1661-1665)
`regs 83 to 87 are repealed and therefore not encoded` MEANS
        "83 [Repealed, SOR/2013-64, s. 2]"
    ... "84 [Repealed, SOR/2013-64, s. 2]"
    ... "85 [Repealed, SOR/2013-64, s. 2]"
    ... "86 [Repealed, SOR/2013-64, s. 2]"
    ... "87 [Repealed, SOR/2013-64, s. 2]"
